# argv Contract

File: docs/argv.oot

The 10 startup flags accepted by `ooda-tui`. Flags set initial state;
runtime control flows through slash commands and keybindings.

## Flags

| Flag | Arg | Effect |
|------|-----|--------|
| `--teamwork` | - | Start with teamwork (multi-agent) mode on |
| `--yolo` | - | Start with yolo (auto-approve all tool calls) on |
| `--cwd` | path | Run as if cwd were `<path>` |
| `--no-color` | - | Disable ANSI codes (for `script` / CI capture) |
| `--provider` | name | Override default provider for this run |
| `--model` | name | Override default model for this run |
| `--theme` | name | Override default theme for this run |
| `--token` | sub [...] | Headless token telemetry; does not open the TUI |
| `--help`, `-h` | - | Print reference, exit 0 |
| `--version`, `-v` | - | Print version, exit 0 |

## Behavior

- Flags are parsed left-to-right. Later flags override earlier ones.
- Unknown flags: print error to stderr, exit 2.
- Missing required arg (`--cwd PATH`, `--provider NAME`, etc.):
  print error to stderr, exit 2.
- `--token <sub> [...]` is a one-shot headless path. Remaining
  argv after `--token` is forwarded to the token cluster and the
  process does not open the TUI.
- Without `--help`, `--version`, or `--token`, the binary opens
  the line-mode TUI session.

## Exit codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| 0 | success |
| 1 | help/version read failure (rare) |
| 2 | usage error (unknown flag, missing arg) |
| 64 | OODACODEX missing or unreadable (fail-closed per §1.5) |
